{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Which the prophet speaks.</b> Likewise the words of Jeremiah in the pericope 'When a prophet speaks' — at the time he speaks, and after he finished explaining the matter of the soothsayers who were in the land. And it is the way of the seventy-three [verses?], he warned not to shed innocent blood in the land. And the meaning is that the land be pure from the abomination of the soothsayers and also not be defiled by innocent blood."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The phrase 'דרך ע״ג' is obscure; 'ע״ג' read hyper-literally as 'the way of 73,' possibly a citation or abbreviation of uncertain meaning. The reference to Jeremiah is to chapter 28 (parashat 'בבא דבר הנביא')."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:57.849254544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}